Patch 0036 (spill24; define nothing, inert until the host calls vglSpillSetKind / vglSetSpillStrictHook). Written against the vp29 tree
(/home/claude/g23/agents/slow24/vgl-new29) and checked with `patch --dry-run` there; not built, not run (no Vita build in this task).
1. Spill counter, always on: every allocation of gpu_alloc_mapped_aligned_for_gpu_inner that missed video memory and was given main RAM,
   phycont, cdlg or newlib memory is counted by kind (other / texture / render target) and pool, with its bytes: vglGetSpillStats(out, 28).
   Textures are filed automatically (gpu_alloc_mapped_for_gpu_tex at the texture storage sites); the host files render targets with
   vglSpillSetKind(2) around their creation (and anything else stays "other"). Cost: a branch and two adds, only on a spill.
2. GXV_VRAM_STRICT: vglSetSpillStrictHook(fn). With a hook set, a texture allocation that finds no video memory calls fn(size) and takes the old
   fallback chain this once. fn only RECORDS a request (no sceGxmFinish, no collector cycle, no log, no frees inside the allocation: it can run in an
   open scene, as patch 0035 removed from glFinish); the host drains its deferred frees at its next present, and the allocations after that find the
   video memory. Without a hook (the default) nothing changes. Stats: [24] tries, [25] new requests recorded, [26] spilled anyway (every try),
   [27] tries that found a request already waiting. Swizzled uploads (vglForceAllocAligned, which the host calls) are filed by the host with
   vglSpillSetKind(1) around the call, so they count as textures and go strict too.

